PRE-FLIGHT
  ├─ Tag all subjects by type: GENERAL | MERGED | REGULAR
  ├─ Sub-tag by state: SCHEDULED | EMPTY
  │     (EMPTY = schedule or room is null) = Locked
  │
  ├─ LOCKED ← all GENERAL subjects (SCHEDULED or EMPTY)
  │     ├─ Visual tag: "General"
  │     └─ EMPTY ones: schedule_missing = true
  │        (included in output; warn admin; GA never touches these)
  │
  ├─ MERGED_GROUPS ← all detected merge sets
  │     ├─ Visual tag: "Original" (for pre-existing merges)
  │     ├─ If all members SCHEDULED → goes into Stage 1
  │     └─ If any member EMPTY → entire group goes to PENDING
  │        as MERGED_NEEDS_GENERATION (scheduled together from scratch)
  │
  └─ PENDING ← everything else, with sub-tags:
        ├─ NEEDS_GENERATION (EMPTY subjects)
        ├─ NEEDS_RESCHEDULE (SCHEDULED but potentially conflicted)
        └─ MERGED_NEEDS_GENERATION (merged group with empty members)


STAGE 1: Fix MERGED_GROUPS
  ├─ For each merged group (all-SCHEDULED only):
  │    ├─ Check conflict against LOCKED
  │    │    └─ If conflict → reschedule group as a unit (GA optimizer)
  │    │       (members must keep shared time + room)
  │    └─ Visual tag preserved: "Original"
  │
  ├─ Then check merged-vs-merged conflicts
  │    └─ Reschedule conflicting groups as units (GA optimizer)
  │
  └─ RESOLVED ← LOCKED ∪ fixed MERGED_GROUPS


STAGE 2+3 LOOP (run as a tight loop, not sequential phases)

  STAGE 2: Triage PENDING
    ├─ For each pending subject:
    │    ├─ If EMPTY → stay in PENDING, skip conflict check
    │    ├─ If SCHEDULED:
    │    │    ├─ Conflict with RESOLVED? → keep in PENDING
    │    │    └─ No conflict? → move to RESOLVED
    └─ Only SCHEDULED subjects can move to RESOLVED here

  STAGE 3: GA Optimizer on PENDING
    ├─ Prepare inputs:
    │    ├─ NEEDS_RESCHEDULE → clear their schedules/rooms
    │    ├─ NEEDS_GENERATION → already blank, ready as-is
    │    └─ MERGED_NEEDS_GENERATION → ready as-is, with
    │        constraint that members share time + room
    │
    ├─ Run GA with RESOLVED as HARD CONSTRAINTS - (New Fix! -(Add the Locked as hard Constraints as well))
    │   (no output can conflict with anything in RESOLVED;
    │    invalid solutions rejected, not just penalized)
    │
    ├─ Validate output using canonical conflict detector:
    │    ├─ Time overlap via interval math
    │    │   (parse start/end → check a_start < b_end AND b_start < a_end)
    │    ├─ Room comparison via set expansion
    │    │   ("1200/1195" → {"1200", "1195"}, check intersection)
    │    ├─ Section + faculty equality checks
    │    ├─ Internal conflicts within new schedule?
    │    ├─ Conflicts against RESOLVED?
    │    └─ Merged groups still merged? (members share time + room)
    │
    ├─ Conflict-free new subjects → move to RESOLVED
    └─ Still-conflicted → back to PENDING

  LOOP CONTROL:
    ├─ If anything moved to RESOLVED this iteration → loop again
    ├─ Else if PENDING is empty → done
    └─ Else if max iterations reached → HUMAN_REVIEW
       reason_type: "unresolvable_conflict"
       (remaining PENDING subjects; returned separately from RESOLVED)


OUTPUT
  ├─ RESOLVED concat with tags preserved:
  │     ├─ "General" — all general subjects (SCHEDULED show schedule; EMPTY show schedule_missing warning)
  │     ├─ "Original" — pre-existing schedules/merges kept as-is
  │     └─ (untagged) — GA-generated or GA-rescheduled
  └─ HUMAN_REVIEW list (returned separately from RESOLVED):
        └─ UNRESOLVABLE subjects (reason_type: "unresolvable_conflict")
           (any remaining conflicts in RESOLVED can only originate from
            LOCKED General subjects, since those are the only items the GA cannot move)


CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS (apply everywhere)
  ├─ ONE canonical conflicts(a, b) function used by:
  │    ├─ Pre-flight tagging
  │    ├─ Stage 1 merged-group checks
  │    ├─ Stage 2 triage
  │    ├─ Stage 3 GA fitness function
  │    └─ Stage 3 post-GA validation
  │
  ├─ Conflict definition (all axes checked together):
  │    Time overlap AND (same section OR room overlap OR same faculty)
  │
  ├─ GA fitness treats conflicts as HARD constraints:
  │    Either reject invalid solutions outright, OR
  │    apply penalty large enough that no soft objective
  │    combination can outweigh a single hard violation
  │
  └─ General subjects (LOCKED) are never modified at any stage